  "kanji": "張",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 張\ntitle: stretch tight; assert\njlpt: 1\ntags: [jlpt-n1, grade-5, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 11\nradical: 弓\nradicalNumber: 57\nonyomi: [チョウ]\nkunyomi: [は.る, -は.り, -ば.り]\nquizOnyomi: [チョウ]\nquizKunyomi: [は.る]\ndistractors: [長, 弧, 弱]\nquiz_exclusions: [伸, 引, 延, 広, 述]\n---\n\n# 張 — stretch tight; assert\n\n**Strokes:** 11 · **Key (radical):** 弓 (no. 57), at the left · **JLPT:** N1 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n張 is pulling something tight or spreading it out, and by extension putting an opinion forward strongly. [緊張](../words/緊張.md) きんちょう is tension or nervousness, [拡張](../words/拡張.md) かくちょう is expansion or extension, [主張](../words/主張.md) しゅちょう is a claim or assertion, and [出張](../words/出張.md) しゅっちょう is a business trip.\n\nThe Daijisen character entry gives two senses: pulled tight without slack or spreading out sideways, as in 張力 ちょうりょく, \"tension; tensile force,\" and putting an opinion forward strongly, as in 誇張 こちょう, \"exaggeration,\" and 主張. It also lists 張 as a counter for strung things such as bows and koto, for hung things such as curtains and mosquito nets, and for sheets of paper or hide.\n\nThe verb 張る はる, \"to stretch; to spread; to strain; to tighten; to put up (e.g. a tent),\" has no word article yet; [張り切る](../words/張り切る.md) はりきる, \"to be in high spirits; to be full of vigor; to be eager,\" is built on it.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** find 弓, \"bow,\" at the left and [長](長.md), \"long, chief,\" at the right. Imagine a bow string pulled long and taut. This is a memory aid only: it makes no claim that 長 contributes meaning or sound. Historical formation is not established here.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| チョウ | on | [緊張](../words/緊張.md) きんちょう — tension; nervousness; [拡張](../words/拡張.md) かくちょう — expansion; extension; [主張](../words/主張.md) しゅちょう — assertion; claim; [出張](../words/出張.md) しゅっちょう — business trip; official trip |\n| は.る | kun | [張り切る](../words/張り切る.md) はりきる — be full of energy; be eager |\n| -は.り | kun | 見張り みはり - watch; guard; lookout; surveillance; 張り紙 はりがみ - notice; poster; the -は.り form occurs inside compounds, not selected for questions here |\n| -ば.り | kun | [欲張り](../words/欲張り.md) よくばり — greedy; a greedy person; 縄張り なわばり - one's turf; territory; the voiced -ば.り form occurs inside compounds, not selected for questions here |\n\nIn 緊張, 緊 supplies キン and 張 supplies チョウ. In 拡張, 拡 supplies カク. In 主張, 主 supplies シュ. In 出張, 出 supplies シュツ, shortened to しゅっ before チョウ.\n\nIn 張り切る, 張り is the stem of the verb 張る, so 張 writes は and り is okurigana, the kana ending that follows the kanji; 切る supplies きる. In 欲張り, 欲 supplies よく and 張り is read ばり, the voiced form of はり. The same voiced ば appears in [威張る](../words/威張る.md) いばる, \"to put on airs; to throw one's weight about; to swagger.\" In [引っ張る](../words/引っ張る.md) ひっぱる, \"to pull; to draw; to pull tight,\" 張る follows the small っ and is pronounced ぱる.\n\nThe official Joyo table, the list of standard-use readings, shows チョウ, with 張力, 拡張 and 主張 as examples, and はる, with 張る, 欲張る and 引っ張る, and sets 貼る beside はる as a contrasting writing. Practice selects チョウ and は.る; the other kun readings are retained from KANJIDIC2 and illustrated with dictionary words. JMdict also lists ばる as a separate suffix entry for the voiced form.\n\n## Common words\n\n- [緊張](../words/緊張.md) きんちょう — tension; nervousness\n- [拡張](../words/拡張.md) かくちょう — expansion; extension\n- [主張](../words/主張.md) しゅちょう — assertion; claim\n- [出張](../words/出張.md) しゅっちょう — business trip; official trip\n- [張り切る](../words/張り切る.md) はりきる — be full of energy; be eager\n- [欲張り](../words/欲張り.md) よくばり — greedy; a greedy person\n- [威張る](../words/威張る.md) いばる — swagger; act arrogantly\n- [引っ張る](../words/引っ張る.md) ひっぱる — pull; tug\n\n## Notes\n\n- [主](主.md), \"master, principal,\" is the other kanji in 主張, and [出](出.md), \"go out, exit,\" is the other kanji in 出張. 緊 in 緊張, 拡 in 拡張 and 威 in 威張る do not have kanji cards yet.\n- [長](長.md), \"long, chief,\" is the right-hand part and also reads チョウ, but it means \"long\" or \"chief,\" not \"stretch tight.\" [弧](弧.md), \"arc; curved line,\" and [弱](弱.md), \"weak; frail,\" also contain a 弓 shape but are not written with 長 at the right.\n- [伸](伸.md), \"stretch; lengthen,\" [引](引.md), \"pull; draw,\" [延](延.md), \"prolong; postpone,\" and [広](広.md), \"wide, spacious,\" each overlap a sense of 張: JMdict glosses 張る as \"to stretch; to spread,\" 引っ張る as \"to pull; to draw,\" and 拡張 as \"expansion; extension; enlargement.\" [述](述.md), \"state; relate,\" overlaps the \"assert\" sense of 主張. All five are kept out of this card's quiz options. Do not treat \"stretch\" or \"assert\" as exclusive to any one character.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-11-02 snapshot. Word identities and spelling restrictions: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1241880, 1205220, 1325910, 1339660, 1427870, 1547390, 1156320, 1601900, 1427900, 2250310, 1630860, 1427820, 1599710, 1623160 and 1267820. Character reading and compounds: [Digital Daijisen, 張](https://www.weblio.jp/content/張).\n\nUsage evidence: [Official Joyo kanji table (2010), PDF p. 109](https://www.bunka.go.jp/kokugo_nihongo/sisaku/joho/joho/kijun/naikaku/pdf/joyokanjihyo_20101130.pdf#page=109).\n",
